        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(zalo): bound proxy fetcher cache to 64 entries",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Zalo retained a process-lifetime Map of proxy fetchers with no bound and no owner-local ProxyAgent cleanup.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nChose ClawSweeper option 1 (Zalo-local lifecycle):\n\n- Cap cache at 64 with insertion-order eviction.\n- Create/dispose ProxyAgents inside Zalo (no core Symbol.for close).\n- Monitor acquires a lease so eviction cannot close a live account agent.\n- Evicted unused entries dispose immediately; retained callers fail closed.\n\nAdditionally:\n- `src/infra/net/proxy-fetch.ts`: Add typed `closeProxyFetch()` lifecycle helper and restore `PROXY_FETCH_CLOSE` mechanism so `makeProxyFetch` wrappers expose a close method for cache owners.\n- `src/plugin-sdk/fetch-runtime.ts`: Export `closeProxyFetch` and `PROXY_FETCH_CLOSE` from the public SDK.\n- `scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.mjs`: Bump public export/callable budgets.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** unbounded proxy fetch wrappers/dispatchers.\n**After:** ≤64 unused cache slots; monitor-held proxies stay alive until stop; disposed fetchers fail closed.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `2dc81985591`\n\nFocused tests: 7 passed.\n\n```\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > returns undefined for empty or whitespace proxy URLs\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > caches fetchers by trimmed proxy URL\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > negative control: Map without bound retains oldest after 65 inserts\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > evicts the oldest proxy fetcher when more than 64 distinct URLs are resolved\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > closes the underlying ProxyAgent dispatcher on unused eviction\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > retained evicted fetcher fails closed and does not recreate a dispatcher\n ✓ |extension-zalo| resolveZaloProxyFetch > defers dispose for leased monitor fetchers until release\n```\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\n\nLow. Lifecycle is Zalo-local. `closeProxyFetch` is an additive SDK export; no existing callers broken.",
